{"id":"html.parser/HTMLParser.handle_entityref","module":"html.parser","qualname":"HTMLParser.handle_entityref","name":"handle_entityref","kind":"method","parent":"html.parser/HTMLParser","signatures":["HTMLParser.handle_entityref(name)"],"doc":"This method is called to process a named character reference of the form &name; (e.g. &gt;), where name is a general entity reference (e.g. 'gt'). This method is only called if convert_charrefs is false.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/html.parser.html#html.parser.HTMLParser.handle_entityref","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/html/parser.py","line":563},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"html.parser/HTMLParser.handle_pi","module":"html.parser","qualname":"HTMLParser.handle_pi","name":"handle_pi","kind":"method","parent":"html.parser/HTMLParser","signatures":["HTMLParser.handle_pi(data)"],"doc":"Method called when a processing instruction is encountered. The data parameter will contain the entire processing instruction. For example, for the processing instruction <?proc color='red'>, this method would be called as handle_pi(\"proc color='red'\"). It is intended to be overridden by a derived class; the base class implementation does nothing.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/html.parser.html#html.parser.HTMLParser.handle_pi","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/html/parser.py","line":579},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"html.parser/HTMLParser.handle_startendtag","module":"html.parser","qualname":"HTMLParser.handle_startendtag","name":"handle_startendtag","kind":"method","parent":"html.parser/HTMLParser","signatures":["HTMLParser.handle_startendtag(tag, attrs)"],"doc":"Similar to handle_starttag(), but called when the parser encounters an XHTML-style empty tag (<img ... />). This method may be overridden by subclasses which require this particular lexical information; the default implementation simply calls handle_starttag() and handle_endtag().","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/html.parser.html#html.parser.HTMLParser.handle_startendtag","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/html/parser.py","line":546},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
